  "description": "The MULTISPORT FITNESS bike has been slimmed down so much that the high-quality aluminium frame weighs just 1,590 grams – so you can really speed up. The smooth seams give the bike a classy, carbon look and represent the highest quality standards. The built-in gear mechanism is a Shimano XT Trekking, one of the highest-quality trekking component groups on the market. This set is known for its robustness, reliability, and durability, making it the first choice for extensive tours. The RockShox Paragon Gold suspension fork expertly absorbs unevenness – a plus on unpaved roads and guaranteed comfort for long tours. The MULTISPORT FITNESS 3 rolls on light and extra stable Rose R Thirty Disc wheels. The Maxxis tyres ensure the right grip and convinces with low rolling friction. Equipped with 180 mm rotors in front as well as 160 mm rotors in the back, the hydraulic Shimano MT200 brakes have a confident grip. You won’t need to worry about having enough brake power in wet conditions. This high-quality outfit is rounded out with especially ergonomic Ergon handles. * approx. 11.3 kg, may vary by up to +/- 5% due to manufacturing tolerances, weight for stone grey/shiny orange frame, 19”, without pedals",
